-- title:
--   Theorem 5.6: lifted JM elements are a JM sequence
-- statement:
--   Let $d\ge2$ and $p,q\ge0$ be integers. On $V^{\otimes p}\otimes V^{*\otimes q}$, $V=\mathbb C^d$, use the physical matrix-image tower $A_0\subset A_1\subset\cdots\subset A_{p+q}$ obtained by adding the primal registers first and then the dual registers. Unused factors carry identities. Let $\mathcal X_k$ be the algebra generated by the centers $Z(A_1),\ldots,Z(A_k)$, and let $J_k$ be the explicit signed swap/contraction sum of Eqs.(85),(86), with parameter $\delta=d$. For a first dual step use $J_1=dI$.
--
--   The lifted operators form a Jucys–Murphy sequence. Explicitly,
--   $$
--   J_k\in\mathcal X_k,\quad \sum_{i=1}^{k}J_i\in Z(A_k),\quad
--   \mathcal X_k=\langle J_1,\ldots,J_k\rangle_{\mathbb C}
--   \qquad(1\le k\le p+q).
--   $$
--   This retains the full additive-centrality and separation requirements of Definition 4.7, enabling interpolation in the physical tower.
-- source:
--   Linear programming with unitary-equivariant constraints, arXiv:2207.05713v2, PDF p. 28, Theorem 5.6: lifted JM elements are a JM sequence

import Definitions.Def_QAlgorithms_Papers_Independent_Claimed50_P02

